    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense enters today with significant momentum, headlined by a core of high-ceiling starters facing favorable matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) stands as our premier play of the day; his matchup against Warren, W (3.99 xERA) is bolstered by an ideal hitting park and a dynamic platoon advantage that elevates his base projection significantly. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) provides a massive spark from the UTIL spot. Despite a slightly negative park factor, the combination of a weak starter in Stock (4.94 xERA) and beneficial wind conditions creates a \"Strong\" efficiency profile that is difficult to fade. **Kyle Tucker** (74.09) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) round out our top-tier tier of producers, both benefiting from favorable park environments and favorable SP skill ratings that suggest high run-scoring potential.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, with **Wade Meckler** (46.94) serving as the most difficult omission. While his leadoff spot and platoon advantage against Pecko make him a respectable depth piece, his lower base efficiency compared to the high-OBP and power profiles of **Andy Pages** (71.03) and **Heliot Ramos** (69.03) forced him into a reserve role to preserve game caps. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**; both are currently \"Lineup Pending,\" and while we have projected them based on historical placement, any late-breaking shifts in the batting order could necessitate a quick pivot. **Miguel Vargas** (52.38) and **Dominic Smith** (51.37) remain in the lineup as steady \"Marginal\" to \"Strong\" contributors, though owners should note that **Miguel Vargas** faces an elite holding pitcher in Holmes, C, which slightly tempers his stolen base upside. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** currently sidelined on the IL, we continue to rely on the depth of **Sam Antonacci** (61.82) to maintain our aggressive stolen base floor.",
